<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  devlab — a RUNNABLE side-by-side build for device passes.

  Why this variant exists. An Odin test device carries a Mimir Release-signed install; local builds are
  signed with the shared debug keystore, so `install -r` over it is impossible and the only alternative
  is an uninstall that destroys the example library, Tomes and settings. The `lab` variant is separate-UID and
  debug-signed, which would have solved it — except `lab` deliberately removes MainActivity
  (`app/src/lab/AndroidManifest.xml`: "A lab install must never become a HOME/launcher candidate or
  start product activities"), so it has no activity to drive and cannot host a UI pass.

  That rule is honoured here, not worked around. What must never happen is a test install becoming a
  HOME or LAUNCHER candidate on a device whose whole point is that Mimir IS the frontend. What is
  merely incidental is being launchable at all. So devlab KEEPS MainActivity and removes every one of
  its intent filters:

    - no android.intent.category.LAUNCHER  -> never appears in the app drawer
    - no android.intent.category.HOME      -> never offered as, or selectable as, the device launcher
    - no android.intent.action.MAIN at all -> nothing can resolve it implicitly

  It is therefore reachable ONLY by explicit component, which is exactly what a scripted device pass
  uses and exactly what a stray tap or a launcher-default prompt cannot do:

      adb shell am start -n com.gruning.mimir.rewrite.devlab/com.gruning.mimir.rewrite.MainActivity

  Unlike `lab`, this variant keeps the product's permissions, providers and services: it is a faithful
  stand-in for the debug build (`initWith(debug)`), because a variant that behaves differently from the
  thing under test is a worse instrument. It is NOT an isolated engine target — that is what `lab` is
  for, and `lab` is unchanged.

  The safety properties above are asserted by `verifyDevlabManifest` in app/build.gradle.kts, not left
  to this comment. If you change this file, that task is what will tell you.
-->
<manifest
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <application>
        <activity
            android:name="com.gruning.mimir.rewrite.MainActivity"
            tools:node="merge">
            <!-- removeAll, not a per-category remove: the merger matches an intent-filter by its whole
                 content, so removing "the LAUNCHER category" would silently stop matching the moment
                 someone edited the filter around it. Dropping every filter is the property we actually
                 want and the only one that cannot rot. -->
            <intent-filter tools:node="removeAll" />
        </activity>
        <!-- The Bottom floor  declares SECONDARY_HOME in main, and a devlab install must not be a
             home candidate on either display. Same treatment as MainActivity: kept, so an explicit component start still
             reaches it, with every intent filter dropped. -->
        <activity
            android:name="com.gruning.mimir.rewrite.CompanionSecondaryHomeActivity"
            tools:node="merge">
            <intent-filter tools:node="removeAll" />
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
